.TH HELPBUOY-RELAY 1 "" "helpbuoy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
helpbuoy-relay \- relay for helpbuoy self-hosted remote support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B helpbuoy-relay serve
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR dir ]
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay agent add
.I name
.I key
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay agent remove
.I name
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay agent list
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay client list
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay client remove
.I fingerprint
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay title
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay instruction
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay hostkey
.br
.B helpbuoy-relay version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B helpbuoy-relay
is the SSH relay of helpbuoy. Agents and the people they help connect to
it on one port; it authenticates their Ed25519 keys and splices their
sessions. The screen and input run end to end over an inner SSH connection
that the relay cannot read.
.PP
.B serve
runs the relay, by default on
.BR :5959 .
The other commands change or show the state directory; a running relay picks
up changes within a second.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " addr"
Address to listen on, as host:port or :port.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " dir"
State directory with the host key, agents and registered clients. Default:
.B $HELPBUOY_RELAY_STATE
if set, else the per-user data directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HELPBUOY_RELAY_STATE
Default state directory. The Debian service sets it to
.IR /var/lib/helpbuoy-relay .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR helpbuoy-relayctl (8)
